---
import { grapheneProjectedDiracMomenta, grapheneZigzagEffective } from '../../../data/part06/ch27GrapheneModels.mjs';
const kInitial = 0.85 * Math.PI;
const initial = grapheneZigzagEffective(kInitial, 1, 14);
const [kMinus, kPlus] = grapheneProjectedDiracMomenta();
const xFromK = (k) => 70 + 300 * (k + Math.PI) / (2 * Math.PI);
---

<figure class="chapter-visual graphene-zigzag" data-graphene-zigzag>
  <figcaption>
    <strong>原创交互模型：zigzag graphene edge 的 momentum-resolved Shockley/SSH 映射</strong>
    <span lang="en">Original interactive model: momentum-resolved Shockley/SSH mapping of a zigzag graphene edge</span>
  </figcaption>

  <div class="chapter-visual__controls">
    <label>
      <span>edge momentum k∥/π | edge momentum</span>
      <input type="range" min="0" max="1" step="0.01" value="0.85" data-gz-k />
      <output data-gz-k-out>0.85</output>
    </label>
  </div>

  <svg viewBox="0 0 760 370" role="img" aria-labelledby="gz-title gz-desc">
    <title id="gz-title">Effective dimer chain for a zigzag graphene ribbon at fixed edge momentum</title>
    <desc id="gz-desc">The left panel marks the projected Dirac points and the edge-state momentum window. The right panel displays the momentum-dependent alternating chain and its analytic edge-state amplitude.</desc>

    <g aria-label="projected edge Brillouin zone">
      <line x1="70" y1="105" x2="370" y2="105" class="gz-axis" />
      <line x1={xFromK(kMinus)} y1="75" x2={xFromK(kMinus)} y2="135" class="gz-dirac" />
      <line x1={xFromK(kPlus)} y1="75" x2={xFromK(kPlus)} y2="135" class="gz-dirac" />
      <line x1="70" y1="105" x2={xFromK(kMinus)} y2="105" class="gz-edge-window" />
      <line x1={xFromK(kPlus)} y1="105" x2="370" y2="105" class="gz-edge-window" />
      <circle cx={xFromK(kInitial)} cy="105" r="9" class="gz-cursor" data-gz-cursor />
      <text x="58" y="145">−π</text><text x="211" y="145">0</text><text x="360" y="145">π</text>
      <text x={xFromK(kMinus) - 14} y="63">K̄′</text><text x={xFromK(kPlus) - 10} y="63">K̄</text>
      <text x="88" y="42">edge-state window in the nearest-neighbour zigzag model</text>
      <text x="88" y="185">orange segments: |2 cos(k∥/2)| &lt; 1</text>
    </g>

    <g aria-label="effective dimer chain">
      <text x="425" y="42">effective double-line chain at fixed k∥</text>
      {Array.from({ length: 6 }, (_, index) => {
        const xA = 430 + index * 48;
        const xB = xA + 20;
        return (
          <g>
            <circle cx={xA} cy="95" r="6" class="gz-site-a" />
            <circle cx={xB} cy="95" r="6" class="gz-site-b" />
            <line x1={xA + 6} y1="95" x2={xB - 6} y2="95" class="gz-bond gz-bond-t1" data-gz-bond-t1 />
            {index < 5 && <line x1={xB + 6} y1="95" x2={xA + 42} y2="95" class="gz-bond gz-bond-t2" data-gz-bond-t2 />}
          </g>
        );
      })}
      <text x="430" y="127">t₁(k∥)=2t cos(k∥/2)</text>
      <text x="430" y="150">t₂=t</text>
      <line x1="420" y1="170" x2="720" y2="170" class="gz-divider" />
      <text x="430" y="196">normalized edge amplitude |Aₙ|</text>
      {initial.amplitudes.map((value, index) => (
        <rect x={430 + index * 20} y={330 - 115 * Math.abs(value)} width="12" height={115 * Math.abs(value)} class="gz-amplitude" data-gz-amplitude={index} />
      ))}
      <line x1="425" y1="330" x2="720" y2="330" class="gz-axis" />
      <text x="675" y="354">double line n</text>
    </g>
  </svg>

  <div class="chapter-visual__readout" aria-live="polite">
    <span data-gz-hoppings>t₁={initial.t1.toFixed(3)}, t₂={initial.t2.toFixed(3)}</span>
    <span data-gz-gap>projected bulk gap proxy = {initial.projectedBulkGap.toFixed(3)}</span>
    <span data-gz-xi>edge localization length = {initial.localizationLength.toFixed(3)} double lines</span>
    <strong data-gz-status>A normalizable zigzag Shockley edge solution exists for this momentum.</strong>
  </div>

  <noscript><p><strong>无 JavaScript 回退 | No-JavaScript fallback:</strong> 初始 $k_\parallel=0.85\pi$ 位于 projected K/K′ 之外的 edge-state window，$|t_1/t_2|&lt;1$，解析 edge amplitude 按 $[-2\cos(k_\parallel/2)]^n$ 衰减。</p></noscript>

  <div class="chapter-visual__contract">
    <p><strong>模型：</strong>最近邻 π-only zigzag ribbon 在固定 <code>k∥</code> 下可重排为 two-site chain，<code>t₁(k∥)=2t cos(k∥/2)</code>、<code>t₂=t</code>。所示终止的零能 Shockley/SSH 解满足 <code>Aₙ₊₁=−(t₁/t₂)Aₙ</code>。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Model:</strong> at fixed <code>k∥</code>, the nearest-neighbour π-only zigzag ribbon can be rearranged into a two-site chain with <code>t₁(k∥)=2t cos(k∥/2)</code> and <code>t₂=t</code>. The zero-energy Shockley/SSH solution for the displayed termination obeys <code>Aₙ₊₁=−(t₁/t₂)Aₙ</code>.</p>
    <p><strong>验收：</strong><code>|k∥|&gt;2π/3</code> 时 <code>|t₁|&lt;|t₂|</code>，解可归一化；在 projected Dirac momenta <code>|k∥|=2π/3</code>，projected bulk gap 闭合且 localization length 发散；接近 zone boundary 时 <code>t₁→0</code>，edge state 局域在最外层 double line。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Acceptance:</strong> for <code>|k∥|&gt;2π/3</code>, <code>|t₁|&lt;|t₂|</code> and the solution is normalizable. At the projected Dirac momenta <code>|k∥|=2π/3</code>, the projected bulk gap closes and the localization length diverges. Near the zone boundary <code>t₁→0</code>, so the edge state localizes on the outermost double line.</p>
    <p><strong>边界：</strong>该图描述无 SOC、最近邻、abrupt zigzag termination 下的 ordinary Shockley edge band。加入 intrinsic SOC 后 K/K′ bulk gap 打开并形成 helical connectivity；真实 edge 还受 second-neighbour hopping、passivation、reconstruction、magnetism 与 interactions 影响。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Boundary:</strong> the figure describes the ordinary Shockley edge band of a nearest-neighbour, no-SOC model with an abrupt zigzag termination. Intrinsic SOC opens the K/K′ bulk gap and produces helical connectivity. A real edge is additionally affected by second-neighbour hopping, passivation, reconstruction, magnetism, and interactions.</p>
  </div>
</figure>

<script>
  import { grapheneZigzagEffective } from '../../../data/part06/ch27GrapheneModels.mjs';
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-graphene-zigzag]').forEach((root) => {
    const kInput = root.querySelector('[data-gz-k]');
    if (!(kInput instanceof HTMLInputElement)) return;
    const setText = (selector, value) => {
      const element = root.querySelector(selector);
      if (element instanceof HTMLElement || element instanceof SVGTextElement) element.textContent = value;
    };
    const update = () => {
      const fraction = Number(kInput.value);
      const k = fraction * Math.PI;
      const model = grapheneZigzagEffective(k, 1, 14);
      const cursor = root.querySelector('[data-gz-cursor]');
      if (cursor instanceof SVGCircleElement) cursor.setAttribute('cx', String(70 + 300 * (k + Math.PI) / (2 * Math.PI)));
      root.querySelectorAll('[data-gz-amplitude]').forEach((bar) => {
        if (!(bar instanceof SVGRectElement)) return;
        const index = Number(bar.dataset.gzAmplitude);
        const height = 115 * Math.abs(model.amplitudes[index] ?? 0);
        bar.setAttribute('y', (330 - height).toFixed(2));
        bar.setAttribute('height', height.toFixed(2));
      });
      root.querySelectorAll('[data-gz-bond-t1]').forEach((line) => {
        if (line instanceof SVGLineElement) line.style.strokeWidth = String(1.5 + 4 * Math.min(Math.abs(model.t1), 2) / 2);
      });
      root.querySelectorAll('[data-gz-bond-t2]').forEach((line) => {
        if (line instanceof SVGLineElement) line.style.strokeWidth = '3.5';
      });
      setText('[data-gz-k-out]', fraction.toFixed(2));
      setText('[data-gz-hoppings]', `t₁=${model.t1.toFixed(3)}, t₂=${model.t2.toFixed(3)}`);
      setText('[data-gz-gap]', `projected bulk gap proxy = ${model.projectedBulkGap.toFixed(3)}`);
      setText('[data-gz-xi]', Number.isFinite(model.localizationLength)
        ? `edge localization length = ${model.localizationLength.toFixed(3)} double lines`
        : 'edge localization length = ∞');
      setText('[data-gz-status]', model.edgeAllowed
        ? 'A normalizable zigzag Shockley edge solution exists for this momentum.'
        : Math.abs(Math.abs(k) - 2 * Math.PI / 3) < 1e-6
          ? 'Projected bulk gap closed at the Dirac projection; the edge solution delocalizes.'
          : 'The displayed termination has no normalizable zero-energy edge solution at this momentum.');
    };
    kInput.addEventListener('input', update);
    update();
  });
</script>

<style>
  .graphene-zigzag svg { width: 100%; max-height: 28rem; }
  .graphene-zigzag text { fill: currentColor; font-size: 13px; }
  .gz-axis, .gz-divider { stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-3); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .gz-dirac { stroke: var(--sl-color-red-high, #b42318); stroke-width: 2; stroke-dasharray: 5 4; }
  .gz-edge-window { stroke: var(--sl-color-text-accent); stroke-width: 7; }
  .gz-cursor { fill: var(--sl-color-accent-high); stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-7); stroke-width: 2; }
  .gz-site-a { fill: var(--sl-color-accent-high); }
  .gz-site-b { fill: var(--sl-color-text-accent); }
  .gz-bond { stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-3); }
  .gz-amplitude { fill: var(--sl-color-text-accent); }
</style>
